{"authorDailyContributionsMap":{"nraisa0408":[{"date":"2026-10-31T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"7811a4e2c66e999f53822da74749b654b63de824","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Point the Command Summary link at the command summary","messageBody":"The site map\u0027s Command Summary link opened the FAQ, as it pointed at\nUserGuide.html#faq, the same target as the FAQ link above it.\n\nLet\u0027s point it at UserGuide.html#command-summary.\n\nFixes #468\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"aa84355681ef57f87c834597a07b504768752290","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Name the intended users at the start of the User Guide","messageBody":"The UG introduction described a generic patient-record app, so a\nfirst-time reader did not learn whom MediConnect is for, although the\nDG\u0027s product scope says so.\n\nLet\u0027s add two sentences, matching the DG\u0027s target user profile and\nvalue proposition: the main and secondary users, and that the app\nkeeps each patient\u0027s care information in one place.\n\nFixes #461\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"27c9eafedd1ead626364e06093beb3ba3e7fca3b","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Say that indices must come before prefixed parameters","messageBody":"The UG said that parameters can be in any order. That holds for\nparameters with a prefix, but INDEX and MED_INDEX must come first,\nin the order shown, e.g., editmed t/08:00 1 2 is rejected.\n\nLet\u0027s state both rules, with an example of each.\n\nFixes #460\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":4,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"67d317cbb66ec27e4db9b82fc5196d66bc39449a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Define the result box and the status message","messageBody":"The UG used \"result box\" once without introducing it, and the DG\u0027s\nmanual tests call the same text the \"status message\", which could be\ntaken for the status bar. The UG also called the detail panel the\n\"details panel\" and the \"view panel\" in one place each.\n\nLet\u0027s name the result box in the Quick start, define the status\nmessage once at the start of the manual-testing appendix, and use\n\"detail panel\" throughout.\n\nFixes #488\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":5,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"871383dc4b018eccc5a9c224bc1ec27a147d4876","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Describe the screenshot, diagrams and photos in alt text","messageBody":"The main screenshot\u0027s alternative text was only \"Ui\", nine DG\ndiagrams had none, and neither had the AboutUs photos or the MarkBind\nlogo in the footer.\n\nLet\u0027s describe what each screenshot and diagram shows, name each\nmember in their photo\u0027s alt text, and mark the footer logo, which\nthe word MarkBind follows, as decorative.\n\nFixes #480\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":17,"deletions":17}}}]}],"akoromy":[],"JellehBelleh":[{"date":"2026-10-31T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"d9a9e1b5316bca00b3daed1d9c0c12d55b9c76ef","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into clarify-saving-guidance","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"fe957af970236b451ce7ad2bd0c893af4ecd1786","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Clarify cleanup for clear recovery tests","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":10,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"cdf6213af59f54fdcbb1dd8116173661f9f79b3a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Clarify backup safety in the User Guide","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":5,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"b6a88b3eb33f8d318777b04e820da5254f2c93d5","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Clarify Quick start prerequisites","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":2,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"a3772bb74e96ae0dea95bffc2e195e8954036e93","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Consolidate contact loading guidance","messag